WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.790
Marc Scott Zicree, Screenwriter/Author: A
lot of people think that “Well they read

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:07.120
the script they really liked it,” that's
meaningless it's like “Did they buy it?”

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.120
“No.”

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:15.780
Film Courage: What do you say to screenwriters
who say it's not their job to get the movie

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:21.859
made it's simply their job to write the script
have an idea and get that out there?

00:00:21.859 --> 00:00:28.900
Marc: Well when people tell me they want to
write a script I say to them do you want to

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:33.340
write a script or do you want to make a movie
because they're two very different things

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.290
and early in my career I was friends with
Charles Joffe who was Woody Allen's agent

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:42.670
and then his producer and I said Charlie and
film and tv where's the power he said in television

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:46.500
it's the writer producer hyphenate ideally
the writer executive producer hyphen at the

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:53.170
showrunner in films it's generally the writer
director hyphenate sometimes a producer but

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:58.170
often the writer director and and that told
me where to go in my career I went into television

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:03.420
because writers run television and so that
meant that what I wrote would get made what

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:10.510
I wrote would get on the screen I’d say
90-95 of what I've written has been shot and

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:15.520
my friends who are screenwriters have lives
of endlessly writing scripts for these other

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:22.690
people who may or may not be unstable but
most of their work doesn't get made and that

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:26.470
I know screenwriters have worked for decades
and none of them they've earned a good living

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:31.560
and none of their work has gotten shot for
me that would be a useless life because my

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:36.270
goal is to create a body of work that moves
an audience that entertains an audience that

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:41.470
is meaningful to them and so you have to know
what what you're trying to accomplish so if

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:45.090
a screenwriter wants to be a screenwriter
doesn't want to be a director doesn't want

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:50.450
to be a producer then yes they can write scripts
but those scripts may not sell or if they

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:54.930
sell they may not get made the way you wanted
them to get made or you may get fired or they

00:01:54.930 --> 00:02:00.930
may be they may sell and be and never get
made so if your goal is to make a living as

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:05.450
a writer there are a lot of different ways
to do that or as an actor or as a director

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:14.440
as a producer but the more you say let's chart
a path that gets my work made and gets me

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:21.390
an income then that's a strategy that allows
you to be much more effective and and I'm

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:25.100
not saying not to have a career as a screenwriter
I have friends who've made millions and millions

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:31.780
of dollars as screenwriters and they've had
some great films made but you're a little

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:39.000
more thrown to the the wins of fate in that
direction so so one thing I would say to anybody

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:44.910
who wants to be a screenwriter is get get
mentors who are successful screenwriters because

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:48.569
you must know what the rules are because they
don't tell you what the rules are generally

00:02:48.569 --> 00:02:52.910
and unless you know what the rules are unless
you know the secret language you will endlessly

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:58.500
be frustrated and the secret language we all
learn it because in order to be successful

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:01.890
you have to know what like when you're in
a room pitching you have to be able to read

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:06.250
the room and it's very funny because I once
Elaine [Zicree] and I once went in and pitched

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:13.060
something with someone who wasn't fair fairly
new to the business and at the end of the

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:17.989
meeting he came out saying well why didn't
you say this and this and this and I said

00:03:17.989 --> 00:03:23.470
because we were saying it but just not in
words we knew you know the person I was pitching

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:26.850
to knew that that was under everything we
were saying and you know and and you also

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:32.700
know what's a yes what to know you know where
you have enthusiasm where you don't there's

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:37.700
there's a lot of ways to read that stuff and
and many of the lessons many people are very

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:41.770
frustrated because they think they're succeeding
when they're not because people in Hollywood

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:45.600
will act like they're enthusiastic they'll
love your script they'll love your idea and

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:50.989
then suddenly they seem to blow a hot and
cold you know and it's because a lot of people

00:03:50.989 --> 00:03:55.190
want to be liked but the moment you're out
of their sight they forget about you and it's

00:03:55.190 --> 00:04:01.840
on to the next thing and so you can never
trust their word and so again that's why you

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:06.260
don't want to a lot of people think that well
they read the script and they really liked

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:13.500
it that's meaningless it's like did they buy
it no but they want me to come in again and

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:18.949
pitch again okay well that's not bad but again
it's sort of like they really liked it but

00:04:18.949 --> 00:04:24.590
they didn't buy it or they you know they when
you go on an audition and they say well that

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:28.189
was great but you know thanks but if they
bring you back yes then you are making an

00:04:28.189 --> 00:04:33.770
impact we have to really look at what a cause
and effect because there are a lot of things

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:39.300
that people feel are symbolic victories that
are actually not moving them forward and a

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:44.550
real victory is when something gets sold when
something gets made once you know and when

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:49.629
they hire you to do the next one you know
it's you can build upon success if you're

00:04:49.629 --> 00:04:54.710
consistently not succeeding then you really
have to look at what's not working and find

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:59.879
out why it's not working but again you need
to have people who will tell you the truth

00:04:59.879 --> 00:05:04.550
but be supportive no one has a right to say
to anybody you'll never make it no one has

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:08.300
the right to say to anybody you don't have
ability you're not you're not good enough

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:12.830
these are irrelevancies the people who succeed
in this business are the ones who are incredibly

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:17.610
persistent my friend Nicholas Meyer who directed
wrath of khan he said the key to success in

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:22.410
Hollywood is persistence with charm because
you need the persistence to get where you're

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:29.020
going and the charm means that they won't
get pissed off at you but but again I know

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:33.469
so many people who think it's like well I've
written 10 scripts and none of them have sold

00:05:33.469 --> 00:05:38.060
well you might try something that you know
I mean again if like often people come to

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:43.610
my round table and they've made like 10 shorts
or 15 shorts I say to them stop making shorts

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:48.680
make a feature because you can't you can't
really make a living doing shorts as far as

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:54.629
I know but if you take several shorts and
link them thematically that can be put together

00:05:54.629 --> 00:06:00.289
into a feature so you can do an ensemble film
made up of shorts if they're linked by a character

00:06:00.289 --> 00:06:07.219
or a theme or or any number of things or a
location and so start thinking that way because

00:06:07.219 --> 00:06:11.471
if a feature is too big to do in one gulp
you might over a course of your be able to

00:06:11.471 --> 00:06:15.840
make three or four shorts put them together
as a feature and bang you're good to go and

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:23.810
so I i think one really has to look at where
one's headed and I think the keys to succeeding

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:30.870
are you have to write from the heart learn
your craft so that means either that doesn't

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:36.860
mean go to go to college necessarily in screenwriting
but it does mean read scripts see why they

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:40.620
work see what works and what doesn't be in
writer's groups where you get feedback but

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:45.360
it has to be supportive that doesn't mean
it's not critical but there's a lot of toxicity

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:51.139
you don't want toxic notes because they don't
help you they just put scars on your heart

00:06:51.139 --> 00:06:56.520
you know and find mentors who do who who whose
work you love who have and who are authentic

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:59.979
because again as I've said before there are
two hollywoods there's a Hollywood of creepy

00:06:59.979 --> 00:07:03.869
horrible people and then there's a Hollywood
of people who are doing the work they love

00:07:03.869 --> 00:07:08.789
they stand by their word they're good family
people and and they're good friends to and

00:07:08.789 --> 00:07:13.259
they're authentic and that's the Hollywood
you want to be part of that's the Hollywood

00:07:13.259 --> 00:07:17.802
you yourself want to represent you do not
have to become a slime ball to make it in

00:07:17.802 --> 00:07:22.080
Hollywood that is there are many many bad
habits that people have you do not have to

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:28.650
a become something you loathe and b I strongly
urge people to avoid working with people they

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:34.710
loathe you will not just have one chance I
mean if you're if you really put your heart

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:40.349
and soul and a work ethic into the into pursuing
this you'll find opportunities you'll make

00:07:40.349 --> 00:07:47.779
opportunities you don't have to be the at
the whim of someone crazy and nor should you

00:07:47.779 --> 00:07:54.039
be and but you also have to decide from the
beginning if you need to be rich because if

00:07:54.039 --> 00:07:59.209
you need to be a millionaire then yes the
studios and the networks are are the the road

00:07:59.209 --> 00:08:03.939
to take if you can if you don't need to be
rich well then there's a million ways to earn

00:08:03.939 --> 00:08:10.029
money writing books writing scripts you can
make films that that earn some money earn

00:08:10.029 --> 00:08:14.240
some money back you can have your own youtube
channel that brings in money from ad revenue

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:18.669
you there's a lot of ways to the Patreon accounts
I mean I know people who are their art is

00:08:18.669 --> 00:08:25.039
being supported by their Patreon accounts
and you know it's just you you need to talk

00:08:25.039 --> 00:08:28.710
to people who are succeeding in the way you
want to succeed and say you don't ask them

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:34.340
for help you don't say get me an agent or
or or open this door for me or or introduce

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:40.890
me to your friends no you ask advice and and
you say how did you do this or what what when

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:44.430
you when this happened what did what what
did you do and and sometimes they'll give

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:48.600
you answers that you can apply and sometimes
they'll give you answers that you can't apply

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:52.650
if you can't apply it then keep asking the
question of different successful people until

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:58.400
you find the answer that you can apply and
and you know but there's there are many different

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:06.240
paths to success and and it's just man you
know Rod Serling used to say I when he when

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:10.410
he would write scripts he would say is this
the truth as I know it or better yet the truth

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:17.930
is I feel it and that's words of wisdom let's
take another scenario and that is someone's

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:23.140
written what they think is an amazing script
it's been purchased and too many hands got

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:28.590
involved and quote messed it up yes and that
happens often in fact I know some writing

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:33.110
team where they wrote a horror script that
they were very proud of and it got went through

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:36.160
all these different writers and they were
very worried about that and finally the writers

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:39.830
guild decided they would have solo writing
credit but then when movie came out it was

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:45.070
really terrible because of all the rewrites
and they were blamed because theirs was the

00:09:45.070 --> 00:09:51.901
only name on it and so you know that's where
I say if you're willing to take power if you're

00:09:51.901 --> 00:09:56.870
willing to take responsibility if you say
I'm going to write and produce and direct

00:09:56.870 --> 00:10:02.160
that doesn't mean you do it alone you're not
a one-man band but it means that you make

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:07.050
sure that what you intended it to be is what
it is you know because the moment you sell

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:10.620
a script then

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:16.450
the moment you sell a script you're at you're
no longer the boss the moment you sell the

00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:23.210
script you're no longer you no longer have
power whoever bought it has power and so it

00:10:23.210 --> 00:10:27.310
can be any number of things anything can happen
to it it's like putting Moses in the little

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:32.450
reed basket and floating him down the nile
you know it's like bye kid I mean will you

00:10:32.450 --> 00:10:37.610
become you know Moses or will you become pharaoh
or will you become like you know joe who shines

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:42.780
the statues you know there's you have no power
over that anymore because you floated him

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:49.360
away that's like what people do with scripts
and so you know when I was a writer on staff

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:53.610
a writer producer story editor one of the
things I would say at the beginning of my

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:58.750
job is I would say my preference is that I
not be rewritten by others I will do as many

00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:05.030
drafts as it takes but I prefer that my work
is what gets to the audience and because I

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:10.090
was a hard worker and a good writer my bosses
honored that it was very rare that I would

00:11:10.090 --> 00:11:21.180
get rewritten and so you know it's you know
you you work harder but you have less sleepless

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:30.400
nights you know so but again it's it's so
easy to shoot stuff now it's so you know I

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:34.560
mean everywhere I turn you know I see people
shooting short films or what or features or

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:40.380
whatever t web series tv shows you know it's
science fiction never predicted that we would

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:48.150
all have video cameras in our pockets and
there's so many benefits of that and you know

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:54.760
fear can stop you laziness can stop you you
really have to say to yourself if I have to

00:11:54.760 --> 00:12:01.500
work hard it's worth it because I want I want
people to know what I'm doing I want to share

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:05.760
this with the world it has to be that because
otherwise if you're going to be half-hearted

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:09.930
about something then go work at McDoogle’s
you know because if the fries are not the

00:12:09.930 --> 00:12:15.680
best fries ever made then it's okay but if
you're going to make movies or tv shows then

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:20.870
then step up there's only when you when you
encounter resistance or adversity you can

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:26.140
either step back or you can step up that's
it those are the only two choices and if you

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:30.560
step back you'll never know what would have
happened if you would just really put your

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:36.610
shoulder to the wheel so you know I my career
has been made by hand and I'm very proud of

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:37.610
that.

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:38.610
Questions For The Viewers:

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:38.625
Do you want to write a script or do you want
to make a movie?

